CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 12
Every Victim has the right to obtain:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. health services in accordance with medical needs;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. special handling related to the confidentiality of the Victim; f. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations; g. guarantee of rights related to status as a Family member as well as a member of the Community; and
h. spiritual guidance services.

Article 38
Forms of behavioral change that can be implemented to carry out Child Protection as referred to in Article 37 paragraph (2) include: a. developing and nurturing the Child in accordance with their abilities, talents, and interests;
b. preventing marriage at child age;
c. caring for, maintaining, educating and protecting the Child;
d. preventing brawls between students;
e. providing opportunities for mothers to provide exclusive breastfeeding for the Child; f. instilling noble character and respect for parents; g. instilling cultural identity, local language, love for the environment; and h. providing special protection to Children in emergency situations, Children in conflict with the law, Children from minority and isolated groups, Children exploited economically and/or sexually, Children who are trafficked, Children who are Victims of narcotics abuse, alcohol, psychotropic substances, and other addictive substances (drugs), Child Victims of kidnapping, sale and trafficking, Child Victims of Violence both physical and/or mental, Children with disabilities, and Child Victims of maltreatment and neglect, Child Victims of HIV/AIDS transmission and Child Victims of social conflict.

